<!--
  Quick Settings tile icon.

  SEPARATE FILE FROM THE NOTIFICATION ICON.
  The tile and the status-bar notification once shared ic_stat_nexus, so branding one would
  have silently changed the other. They are different surfaces with different size budgets:
  a tile draws at roughly the full 24dp, a status-bar icon is scaled down further. Each now
  has its own drawable - the notification uses ic_notification_nexus.xml, which carries the
  same emblem simplified for the smaller size.

  SAME EMBLEM AS THE LAUNCHER ICON.
  Every pathData string below is copied verbatim from ic_launcher_monochrome.xml - the X, the
  triangle, the three nodes and the core. Nothing was redrawn, so the tile and the launcher
  icon cannot drift into two different marks. Only two things differ, and both are forced by
  the size:

    THE TRANSFORM. The source draws in a 512-unit space on a 108dp canvas. A tile icon is
    24dp, so the same artwork is re-centred and rescaled here: translate to the middle of the
    24dp box, scale by 0.072, then shift the artwork's own centre (256, 228 - the midpoint of
    its full extent including the node circles and the X's overshoot below the triangle base)
    to the origin. That leaves roughly 1.5dp of clear space on every side, which the system
    needs for its own padding.

    THE STROKE WEIGHTS. 22 -> 34 for the X and 10 -> 26 for the triangle. At 0.072 the
    original weights would render at 1.6dp and 0.7dp; the triangle in particular would be a
    hairline that all but vanishes once the status bar downscales it. The new values land at
    ~2.4dp and ~1.9dp. The fills (nodes, core) keep their original radii, so the emblem's
    proportions are unchanged - only the lines are heavier, which is what small sizes need.

  FLAT AND SINGLE-COLOUR, LIKE THE NOTIFICATION ICON AND FOR THE SAME REASON.
  Quick Settings repaints the icon according to tile state - accent when active, dim when
  inactive - so colour, gradients and detail in the source are discarded. Only the alpha
  channel survives. A full-colour logo here would render as a solid blob.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24"
    android:tint="#FFFFFFFF">
    <group android:translateX="12" android:translateY="12">
        <group android:scaleX="0.072" android:scaleY="0.072">
            <group android:translateX="-256" android:translateY="-228">
                <!-- The X -->
                <path
                    android:strokeColor="#FFFFFFFF"
                    android:strokeWidth="34"
                    android:strokeLineCap="round"
                    android:pathData="M160,160 L352,352"/>
                <path
                    android:strokeColor="#FFFFFFFF"
                    android:strokeWidth="34"
                    android:strokeLineCap="round"
                    android:pathData="M352,160 L160,352"/>
                <!-- Upward triangle -->
                <path
                    android:strokeColor="#FFFFFFFF"
                    android:strokeWidth="26"
                    android:strokeLineCap="round"
                    android:strokeLineJoin="round"
                    android:pathData="M256,135 L360,315 L152,315 Z"/>
                <!-- Nodes -->
                <path android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF" android:pathData="M256,135 m-30,0 a30,30 0 1,0 60,0 a30,30 0 1,0 -60,0"/>
                <path android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF" android:pathData="M152,315 m-30,0 a30,30 0 1,0 60,0 a30,30 0 1,0 -60,0"/>
                <path android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF" android:pathData="M360,315 m-30,0 a30,30 0 1,0 60,0 a30,30 0 1,0 -60,0"/>
                <!-- Core -->
                <path android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF" android:pathData="M256,256 m-36,0 a36,36 0 1,0 72,0 a36,36 0 1,0 -72,0"/>
            </group>
        </group>
    </group>
</vector>
